{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/557321-what-is-the-ground-made-of-in-the-hisil","id":557321,"title":"What is the ground made of in the Hisil?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-16T14:23:35-07:00","id":557321,"title":"What is the ground made of in the Hisil?","content":"Is everything in Shadow a spirit? Or can sometimes the landscape just be, well, the landscape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T14:46:45-07:00","id":557396,"title":"","content":"Someone can correct me if I'm wrong, but I'm pretty sure you're standing on Gaia, the spirit of the Earth (go planet!). But literally, I'm pretty sure you're standing on a giant celestial spirit of Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T15:00:07-07:00","id":557416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/557321-what-is-the-ground-made-of-in-the-hisil?p=557396#post557396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone can correct me if I'm wrong, but I'm pretty sure you're standing on Gaia, the spirit of the Earth (go planet!). But literally, I'm pretty sure you're standing on a giant celestial spirit of Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>More accurately, slumbering members of her Umia.<br /> <br /> Or if you want to get extremely granular, the quiescent corpus of whichever Location Spirit has the most power in the region, so in a city with a very strong mono-culture, like say, Tokyo, you'd be walking on Ed\u014d itself, while in Midtown, Manhattan, you'd have Spirit for every major street and neighborhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T15:01:52-07:00","id":557417,"title":"","content":"What are you breathing in the Hisil?<br /> Are you breathing at all?<br /> If you are breathing, are you consuming spirits?<br /> If you are not breathing, how do you speak?<br /> If you are forcing spirits in and out of your body (but not eating them), how do they feel about that? o.O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T15:41:58-07:00","id":557459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/557321-what-is-the-ground-made-of-in-the-hisil?p=557417#post557417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you breathing in the Hisil?<br /> Are you breathing at all?<br /> If you are breathing, are you consuming spirits?<br /> If you are not breathing, how do you speak?<br /> If you are forcing spirits in and out of your body (but not eating them), how do they feel about that? o.O</div> </div> </div> </div>MorpheusWhatIfIToldYou.jpg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T15:48:24-07:00","id":557464,"title":"","content":"The air is also Gaia. She's the spirit of Earth, not just the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T15:51:19-07:00","id":557468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/557321-what-is-the-ground-made-of-in-the-hisil?p=557417#post557417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you breathing in the Hisil?<br /> Are you breathing at all?<br /> If you are breathing, are you consuming spirits?<br /> If you are not breathing, how do you speak?<br /> If you are forcing spirits in and out of your body (but not eating them), how do they feel about that? o.O</div> </div> </div> </div>'Bout the same as they usually do. It's business as usual.<br /> <br /> To be fair, the air spirits you're converting with your breath don't have large enough identities to scream much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T22:40:35-07:00","id":557912,"title":"","content":"I perceive the Hisil as being made out of ephemeral, but not necessarily all of that ephemeral is alive. Essence that settles in the Hisil without getting consumed by spirits still takes on the image of the thing that generated it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T22:46:19-07:00","id":557915,"title":"","content":"I also had an idea of calling the atmosphere of the Hisil the Etherspace. It is basically the dimensional space of the Hisil that ephemeral is generated in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T23:52:09-07:00","id":557949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nuwisha Nutjob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/557321-what-is-the-ground-made-of-in-the-hisil?p=557912#post557912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I perceive the Hisil as being made out of ephemeral, but not necessarily all of that ephemeral is alive. Essence that settles in the Hisil without getting consumed by spirits still takes on the image of the thing that generated it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea. When literally everything in the Hisil is a spirit, it begins to seem kind of cluttered. Having a sort of background radiation of ambient ephemera (which may potentially form a spirit if fed Essence) is a bit more grokable to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T07:56:44-07:00","id":558252,"title":"","content":"Everything in the Hisil is a spirit, but that doesn't mean we're dealing with intelligent spirits here. Most of them will be the real world equivalent of bacteria. They're everywhere, but so tiny and unimportant to daily life that its just in the background. For the most part, we don't need to think of them as alive, or even as distinct entities. From an animistic standpoint, they're all alive as spirits. From a realistic standpoint? If its slumbering, its just background filler or a generic object. A slumbering tree spirit is no different from a material world tree, a slumbering rock spirit is no different from a real world rock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-17-2015, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:12:00-07:00","id":558528,"title":"","content":"Unless something has changed in 2e, everything in the hisil is composed of a substance called Ephemera. A sizable portion, perhaps even the bulk, of spirits are dormant and will behave more or less like their earthly counterparts unless they're awoken somehow. Gaia, as far as anyone in the world of darkness can tell, only exists theoretically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:30:16-07:00","id":558539,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of weirdness in the Hisil that the books don't really cover, or even really get into much. The virus spirits are an interesting example, even other spirits don't know where they belong, and consider them aberrations. Just like in real life, we don't even know if they're alive or not.<br /> <br /> Ephemera seems to be just a catch-all term for, 'I don't know what it is, but it isn't made of matter.'<br /> <br /> But yeah, you're either standing on Gaea, or a layer of dormant spirits of dirt and soil and earth on top of another layer of dormant spirits, or as someone pointed out above, a location spirit. It's probably worth noting that higher-ranked spirits tend to have their own secret realm in the Hisil, a place-that-isn't, as opposed to just being in the locale of the Hisil's version of their source. This is how you can have powerful spirits of very common things, like Destruction, that aren't in all places where destruction is occurring. Instead, it has its own lair someplace and its court and members of its court have their own hierarchy and lesser spirits all the way down. Though, it seems, in the current world one of the major spirits of Destruction is in Basra. So while you might be standing on those lesser spirits, you're not necessarily standing on Gaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-17-2015, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T14:04:40-07:00","id":558667,"title":"","content":"You know, I would go so far as to ask... Does it really matter what it is made of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T14:11:39-07:00","id":558692,"title":"","content":"While like everything, there should be different options available, the question is something worth asking.<br /> <br /> A werewolf or human who is respectful of spirits might want to know if they're walking on spirits as they travel the Hisil. And anyone might need to know if it's possible to use Awaken Spirit on the ground beneath an enemy or yourself. Other innovative uses might pop up, for instance using Shadow Masquerade to avoid notice by other spirits by appearing as a dormant 'ground' spirit. The answer to the question helps the Storyteller maintain the integrity of their setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:08:28-07:00","id":558785,"title":"","content":"I'm faaaaairly sure the ground is made of sleeping earth spirits (or road spirits, or building spirits, or whatever it is you're standing on). I would not bank on it being Gaea; Gaea is purely hypothetical, which it wouldn't be if you could use various powers directly on the ground you're standing on to ping it.<br /> <br /> If Gaea exists at all, it's probably much deeper than all the random shite and debris that's accumulated on the planet's surface over the aeons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:13:10-07:00","id":558789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/557321-what-is-the-ground-made-of-in-the-hisil?p=558785#post558785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm faaaaairly sure the ground is made of sleeping earth spirits (or road spirits, or building spirits, or whatever it is you're standing on). I would not bank on it being Gaea; Gaea is purely hypothetical, which it wouldn't be if you could use various powers directly on the ground you're standing on to ping it.<br /> <br /> If Gaea exists at all, it's probably much deeper than all the random shite and debris that's accumulated on the planet's surface over the aeons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would put Gaia as being in a Place That Doesn't Exist, or being housed in the very core of the planet itself.<br /> <br /> On another note, I find the idea of an Ithaeur accidentally waking up the ground spirits for a several-mile radius rather hysterical to think about.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ow! Ow! Ow! We're down here, you know! Your claws are sharp!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;OW! MY EYE!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;OW! That WASN'T an eye!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T19:31:18-07:00","id":558995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/557321-what-is-the-ground-made-of-in-the-hisil?p=558539#post558539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how you can have powerful spirits of very common things, like Destruction, that aren't in all places where destruction is occurring.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact that predation or other lasting destruction is the only means of clearing spiritual remnants \u2014 storm spirits are powerful and dangerous because the ones that live long enough to gain awareness are the ones that eat their fellows and vanish to the (perpetually overcast) skies when they fall to dormancy. A spirit with no local predators can ostensibly sleep for a very long time in the absence of especially desperate or omnivorous scavengers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T23:50:25-07:00","id":561632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/557321-what-is-the-ground-made-of-in-the-hisil?p=557417#post557417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you breathing in the Hisil?<br /> Are you breathing at all?<br /> If you are breathing, are you consuming spirits?<br /> If you are not breathing, how do you speak?<br /> If you are forcing spirits in and out of your body (but not eating them), how do they feel about that? o.O</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, this is something that happens IRL that the Hisil captures <i>extremely</i> well when you notice.<br /> <br /> Millions of births and deaths happen around us every minute. Even if you ignore the lifeforms too small to see, if you ignore all the insects, think about exactly what's happening when you walk across a grass lawn. Every one of those blades is an individual life.<br /> <br /> You're a human. The life and death of even blades of grass is beneath your notice.<br /> You're a Uratha. The life and death of mere mostly-asleep motes is beneath your notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:50:22-07:00","id":563460,"title":"","content":"Going back to 1st ed, things can have spiritual reflections without being Spirits themselves, and are made of ephemera. The distorted buildings and roads, some are Spirits waiting to consume, others are just ephemeral reflections of places that are, were or are soon to be, others are places that aren't with no corresponding reflection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}